# The script `mise run ffi-test` has the editor's headless mode run against
# the config in `config/`, to list commands in the command prompt
# (`execute-command`), to run a command through it that asks in turn, and to
# run a command of config's that names a declaration of the prompt's module.
# What it prints must be exactly `expected`. It touches no file.

reload
settle

# `execute-command`, called with no name, asks `Command: ` with every
# registered command's name as its candidates. Config's style `starts` keeps
# those the text starts, in the order they were registered: with `zz-`
# typed, config's `zz-other`, shown with the key that reaches it, `SPC f f`,
# then `zz-mine`, which no key reaches. `<Escape>` cancels.
run execute-command
commit zz-
scene
key <Escape> Escape -

# The command accepted runs as a step of its own with no argument, so
# `load-theme`, which asks for its own, asks in turn; config's theme,
# `zz-dark`, accepted there, is the one in force: the scene line ends with
# its name. No key is bound to either command.
run execute-command
commit load-theme
key <Enter> Enter -
commit zz-dark
key <Enter> Enter -
scene

# Config's command that names `ExecuteCommand.label` says the prompt's
# label in the echo area: config reaches the command prompt's module.
run prompt-label
scene
